<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Gilboa posts 2H pre-excepts loss, no div.</title>
<headline>Gilboa posts 2H pre-excepts loss, no div.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Second half year ended June 30 vs 18 months to June 30, 1995</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Loss for period</p>
<p>    - pre-excepts	   1.96	  vs none</p>
<p>    - post excepts	  2.39	  vs 13.01</p>
<p>    Exceptional loss	0.43	  vs 13.01</p>
<p>Accumulated deficit</p>
<p>- at beginning of period</p>
<p>				  21.59	 vs 8.58</p>
<p>    - at end of period    23.98	 vs 21.59</p>
<p>Full Name: Gilboa Properties Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE - Gilboa's year end is December 31, hence a second interim report is necessary, directors said.</p>
<p>They said a number of property projects which had not been successful had been abandoned and the costs thereof, together with an apportionment for interest, written off resulting in a loss for the year.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
